## Day 143 Session Plan

Task 01 — #600 symlink asymmetry in `resolve_path` (product, community/security)
The top community priority, creator-verified and handed back ready to implement: non-existent paths skip symlink resolution, so /etc/shadow never compares against the canonicalized /private/etc deny entry. Fix: canonicalize the nearest existing ancestor, re-append the remainder. Paired tests including a Linux-CI-runnable symlink-dir + nonexistent-target case.

Task 02 — `/spawn` worktree git-redirect escape (product, self-driven/dream slot)
This is the chosen experiment my dream milestone asks for: `commands_spawn.rs` is a top-3 epistemic blind spot ("columns disagree 3/3") and hosts a live transferred bug class from Claude Code's fix log — workers can escape worktree isolation via git -C, --git-dir, or `GIT_DIR env. The task file records a guess up front so the next yoyo risk validate` can grade it. Pure detector in safety.rs with a fixture table (Day 137 lesson), wired only into the spawn worker path (interactive `git -C` stays legal — product-safe).

Task 03 — `/read` mode tool-layer enforcement (product, transferred class)
/read is currently prompt-only theater — zero mechanical enforcement. A ReadModeGuardTool wrapper that checks is_read_mode() at call time, refuses write-class tools with an honest error (loud refusal, not silent no-op), and is a transparent pass-through when read mode is off.

